Code

Set up CSS
```{=html}
&lt;style&gt;
  lord-icon {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
  }
  .block {
    background: #e8e8e8;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 20px;
    display: block;
    width: 200px;
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .block:hover {
    box-shadow: 0 4px 18px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 10%);
    color: var(--palette-primary);
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
```


Set up div and icon with target
```{=html}
  &lt;div class="block"&gt;
    &lt;div class="icon"&gt;
```
{{&lt; li lbjtvqiv trigger=click target=.block state=morph-unlocked &gt;}}
```{=html}
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Click here to trigger.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
```

Approach 1: Global CSS via HTML chunk
To quickly style all the icons on the page, you can style the lord-icon element. There are two main ways to accomplish this. First is to add an HTML chunk with the &lt;style&gt; element to your .qmd file.

Code
Added to .qmd file
```html
&lt;style&gt;
  lord-icon {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    border: 1px solid blue;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
```
{{&lt; li laqlvddb &gt;}} {{&lt; li surcxhka &gt;}}



Demo

Approach 2: Global CSS via .css File
The second option for global styling is to create a separate .css file that you link to via the Quarto document’s YAML header. Again, we style the lord-icon element.

Code
Added to styles.css
lord-icon {
  width: 100px;
  height: 100px;
  border: 1px solid blue;
}

Added to .qmd header
---
format: 
  html:
    css: styles.css
---
{{&lt; li laqlvddb &gt;}} {{&lt; li surcxhka &gt;}}



Demo

Approach 3: CSS Classes
To style groups of icons on a page, you can create CSS styles and assign individual icons one or more classes via the class argument. In the example below, we create two classes that control the icon size and border and then apply each class to two icons.

Code
Added to .qmd file
```html
&lt;style&gt;
  lord-icon.smaller {
    width: 50px;
    height: 50px;
    border: 1px dashed red;
  }
  lord-icon.larger {
    width: 75px;
    height: 75px;
    border: 1px solid green;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
```

{{&lt; li laqlvddb class=smaller &gt;}} {{&lt; li surcxhka class=smaller &gt;}} {{&lt; li laqlvddb class=larger &gt;}} {{&lt; li surcxhka class=larger &gt;}}


Demo

Approach 4: Shortcode Style
To style individual icons in-place with no need for the HTML chunk or .css file, you can put styling directly into the style argument.

Code
{{&lt; li laqlvddb style=width:50px;height:50px;border:0; &gt;}}
{{&lt; li laqlvddb style=width:100px;height:100px;border:0; &gt;}}


Demo

Trigger
The trigger argument controls which event plays an icon’s animation. The supported values are in, click, hover, loop, loop-on-hover, morph, boomerang, and sequence. With no trigger, the icon simply rests on its first frame.







Shortcode
Icon




{{&lt; li jjoolpwc &gt;}} (no trigger)



{{&lt; li jjoolpwc trigger=in &gt;}}



{{&lt; li jjoolpwc trigger=click &gt;}}



{{&lt; li jjoolpwc trigger=hover &gt;}}



{{&lt; li jjoolpwc trigger=loop &gt;}}



{{&lt; li jjoolpwc trigger=loop-on-hover &gt;}}



{{&lt; li jjoolpwc trigger=morph &gt;}}



{{&lt; li jjoolpwc trigger=boomerang &gt;}}

State
Many icons bundle several named animation states. Select one with the state argument (browse an icon’s states on the lordicon.com website). For local files, state needs a Raw export, which carries every animation; the smaller Minified export keeps only the one chosen in the editor. See Source.







Shortcode
Icon




{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=morph state=morph-mantion &gt;}}



{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=morph state=morph-neighbourhood &gt;}}



{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=loop state=loop-3d-roll &gt;}}



{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=loop state=loop-smoke &gt;}}

Delay
Looping animations can pause between each loop for a set number of milliseconds using the delay argument.







Shortcode
Icon




{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=loop  &gt;}}



{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=loop delay=3000 &gt;}}

Speed
The speed argument multiplies the playback rate. Values below 1 play in slow motion; values above 1 play faster.







Shortcode
Icon




{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=loop speed=0.5 &gt;}}



{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=loop &gt;}}



{{&lt; li laqlvddb trigger=loop speed=2 &gt;}}

Colors
colors recolors an icon. Outline icons usually have just a primary and secondary color, while flat and lineal icons can have many more. Give each color in rank:color form (ranks are primary, secondary, tertiary, …) and separate multiple colors with commas. Colors accept HTML color names or hex codes.







Shortcode
Icon




{{&lt; li rehjpyyh &gt;}}



{{&lt; li rehjpyyh colors=primary:gold &gt;}}



{{&lt; li rehjpyyh colors=secondary:gold &gt;}}



{{&lt; li rehjpyyh colors=primary:gray,secondary:orange &gt;}}



{{&lt; li rehjpyyh colors=primary:#4030e8,secondary:#ee66aa &gt;}}

Stroke
stroke sets how thick the lines of a (supported) icon are: light, regular, or bold.







Shortcode
Icon




{{&lt; li rehjpyyh stroke=light &gt;}}



{{&lt; li rehjpyyh stroke=regular &gt;}}



{{&lt; li rehjpyyh stroke=bold &gt;}}
